<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reza Abbasi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1565–<a href="/years/1635">1635</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reza Abbasi was a leading Persian painter and calligrapher active at the court of the Safavid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>. He is celebrated for single-figure studies and graceful line drawings that influenced later Persian painting. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> name him among the masters under whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-miniature">Persian miniature</a> painting achieved its mature form.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reza-abbasi.jpg" alt="Reza Abbasi" width="285" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muin Musavvir · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_the_artist_Reza_%27Abbasi_by_Mu%27in_Musavvir,_Isfahan,_Iran,_signed_and_dated_19_April_1676.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…and Milan; miniature painting flourished, first in Tahmasp I's celebrated Shahnameh and later in the single-page works of <b>Reza Abbasi</b>; and Isfahan's ensemble of Naqsh-e Jahan Square, the Shah Mosque, the Sheikh Lotfollah Mosque and the Ali Qapu palace represents one of the supreme achievements of Islamic urban…</blockquote><a href="/empire/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=32.65,51.68&amp;year=1610" aria-label="Isfahan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5876 977 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Reza Abbasi"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6326 1247h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6326 1247h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=32.65,51.68&amp;year=1610">What was here in 1610? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
